《International Olympic Committee consensus statement: methods for recording and reporting of epidemiological data on injury and illness in sport 2020 (including STROBE Extension for Sport Injury and Illness Surveillance (STROBE-SIIS))》：方法与研究设计的原文依据。

【Data collection methods · s9-p1】The methods underpinning the data collection have great impact on the outcome of sport injury and illness surveillance studies.42 81 82 A systematic review of ongoing injury surveillance systems in sport found that data quality aspects were published for only 7 of the 15 systems and validation studies for only 4.83 The review concluded that data quality could be improved through the establishment of data collection standards.

